  <section id="business-across-zones" class="content-section reveal" aria-label="Business Across U.S. Time Zones">
    <h2>8. Business Across U.S. Time Zones</h2>
    <p>
      Coordinating business operations across the United States requires scheduling tools and protocol guidelines:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Remote Work Alignment</strong>: Distributed teams establish "core hours" (typically 12:00 PM to 4:00 PM Eastern Time), which represents the window where Eastern and Pacific business hours overlap.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Stock Markets</strong>: The NYSE and NASDAQ operate on Eastern Time. West Coast traders must align schedules, with markets opening at 6:30 AM Pacific Time.
      </li>
    </ul>

